# frontend/Dockerfile's build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything not
# excluded here gets baked into the image build context as-is. This file
# exists specifically to stop host-machine build artifacts (particularly
# .dart_tool/, which embeds absolute host filesystem paths into
# .dart_tool/package_config.json) from overwriting the fresh, correct
# versions `RUN flutter pub get`/`RUN flutter build web` generate inside
# the container. Hit in practice 2026-08-08: a Windows prod host that had
# previously run `flutter build web --release` locally (see DECISIONS.md,
# "ProdRelease.bat" section) left a Windows-path-poisoned .dart_tool/ on
# disk; without this file, `COPY . .` copied it into the Linux build
# context, clobbering the container's own .dart_tool/, and `flutter
# gen-l10n`'s internal `dart format` step failed trying to open
# `/C:/Users/.../flutter_lints-6.0.0/lib/flutter.yaml` — a Windows path
# misread as a POSIX one.
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
build/
coverage/

# Version control / editor / OS cruft — never useful inside the image
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
